    "evidence_ids": 14,
    "report": {
      "assessment_status": "completed",
      "conclusion": "partial",
      "summary": "The alert is explained by a real but short burst of checkout PlaceOrder server-span failures. The 5-minute PlaceOrder error ratio (rate of STATUS_CODE_ERROR divided by all PlaceOrder server spans) was 0.0 at every 60s step from 03:53:54Z to 04:45:54Z, then rose to 0.6667 at 04:46:54Z, 0.8182 at 04:47:54Z and 0.9333 at 04:48:54Z (evidence ea70e743-cfcd-4f9f-a842-9001538bf43a-t0:a104286e-cfa7-4c29-9b1e-f610bac5944d), matching the 93.33% in the alert annotation and exceeding the 0.5 threshold when the alert fired at 04:48:54Z. The failing PlaceOrder spans carry rpc.grpc.status_code=13 with description 'failed to charge card: ... Payment request failed. Invalid token. app.loyalty.level=gold'; the only checkout client dependency returning a non-zero status is oteldemo.PaymentService (rpc_grpc_status_code=2), while cart, currency, product-catalog and shipping client calls stay at status 0 (0f4e7d01-b492-41bd-8c16-49081ae32e86-t0:fb5c1f33-1210-4813-ad20-953077281bb7, 0f4e7d01-b492-41bd-8c16-49081ae32e86-t2:374ee4e0-5c20-4ea1-82b9-dc814481470b). Payment's own server span grpc.oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge carries STATUS_CODE_ERROR at the same instants (3b2b4e67-4c5e-4345-a0fb-03662f1ae4a9-t0:4190ca34-a71b-42aa-bf32-4ed7e5305821). So the ratio breach is genuine and traceable to payment Charge rejecting the request; the ultimate reason payment rejects ('Invalid token', charge.js:37) remains a hypothesis, and absolute counts are only approximate because window-length increase() totals are mutually inconsistent."
    }
  },
